`sshfs` is used to mount a filesystem from a remote drive at local mount point.

sshfs -o allow_other user@hostname:/home/path /mnt/mountpoint

allow_other is not premitted in most of linux operation by default 

1. sudo vim /etc/fuse.conf

2. uncomment user_allow_other

Making a mounting file
======================

sudo mkdir -p /mnt/mntfile

Changing Premission
===================

sudo chown user:user /mnt/mntfile

sshfs -o allow_other user@hostname:/home/path /mnt/mountpoint

Example:-
=========

sudo vim /etc/fuse.conf

use_allow_other

sudo mkdir -p /mnt/scripting

sudo chown docky:docky /mnt/scripting

sshfs -o allow_other ubuntu:/home/satish-kumar-peddi/Bashscripting /mnt/scripting


